        "max_brightness": 25,
        "default": {
            "val": 25,
            "speed": 128
        },
        "animations": {
            "breathing": true,
            "cycle_all": true,
            "cycle_left_right": true,
            "cycle_up_down": true,
            "solid_color": true,
            "static_gradient": true
        },
        "split_count": [31, 36],
        "_comment": [
            "default.speed 128: qmk lint reports this as 'duplicates the default',",
            "but that 128 comes from the JSON schema — the C default in",
            "quantum/rgb_matrix/rgb_matrix.h is UINT8_MAX/2 = 127, and the schema",
            "value is never emitted. Dropping the line silently changes the speed,",
            "so keep it and ignore that one lint warning.",
            "",
            "x/y are the LED's physical position on the WHOLE assembled board, in",
            "QMK's fixed coordinate space: x 0..224 = left edge..right edge,",
            "y 0..64 = top row..bottom row. They are NOT pixels and NOT per-half.",
            "Effects that sweep or gradient (cycle_left_right, static_gradient,",
            "cycle_up_down, ...) index straight off these numbers, so the two",
            "halves must occupy DIFFERENT x ranges or the animation runs twice,",
            "mirrored, instead of once across the board.",
            "Mapping used: key column 0..16 (see layouts.LAYOUT) -> x = col * 14,",
            "so the left half lands on 0..84 and the right half on 126..224.",
            "Matrix row 0..4 -> y = row * 16.",
            "The ORDER of the entries is the physical WS2812 wiring chain and must",
            "not be reordered; the first 31 are the left strip, the next 36 the right."
        ],
